WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.010
Night, on the hills near Bethlehem.

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.860
An angel brings shepherds
good news of great joy.

3
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.940
Forty days later, in
the Temple in Jerusalem,

4
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.890
an old man named Simeon
sees the child and sings.

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:19.670
An elderly prophetess, Anna, speaks of the
child to everyone waiting for redemption.

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.620
Luke's Gospel opens in the
Temple, and it ends there too.

7
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.980
Why would Luke tell it this way,
with such unexpected witnesses?

8
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.500
In this mission, you'll set
two births side by side:

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.090
John's and Jesus', each
announced, born and named.

10
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:40.570
Then you'll test the history, with
a census that seems not to fit.

11
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.470
Your mission: find out why Luke's
story begins and ends in the Temple,

12
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.200
with shepherds and old
prophets as witnesses.
